  "body": "On [w3cschools](https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_eventattributes.asp) page there is a nice section about Media Events:\r\n\r\n> Events triggered by medias like videos, images and audio (applies to all HTML elements, but is most common in media elements, like `<audio>`, `<embed>`, `<img>`, `<object>`, and `<video>`).\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, `<img>` don't support `onprogress` and to track the progress we must use `XMLHttpRequest` as shown [here](https://stackoverflow.com/a/22593907/965722)\r\n\r\nBecause I didn't find a good explanation of why this event isn't supported by `<img>` tag I'd like to ask for it here.\r\n\r\nAre there any contraindications to add this event to `<img>` tag?\r\n\r\nREF: https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/1698",
